<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pshemakho Kotsev</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1884">1884</a>–<a href="/years/1962">1962</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pshemakho Kotsev was a Kabardian politician who led the government of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mountainous-republic-of-the-northern-caucasus">Mountainous Republic of the Northern Caucasus</a> in 1918–1919. He sought a federal democratic state of the mountain peoples, independent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, but the republic was crushed between the Bolsheviks and Denikin's White army. He emigrated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, where he died.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pshemakho-kotsev.jpg" alt="Pshemakho Kotsev" width="320" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%9A%D0%BE%D1%86%D0%B5%D0%B2_%D0%9F%D1%88%D0%B5%D0%BC%D0%B0%D1%85%D0%BE.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
